Haunt (48181) is an instant-cast, no-cooldown button for Affliction warlocks
holding class perk 910157. The cast time is zeroed per-cast for perk holders
only; other warlock specs keep the real 1.5 sec cast.

Touches: src/server/game/Spells/Spell.cpp -- Spell::prepare() adds a
LivingGear_SpellIsInstantCast() consultation immediately after the
CHEAT_CASTTIME override, plus the forward declaration beside
LivingGear_SpellIsFreeCast.

Why: the Affliction perk previously had no castable ability at all (reports
#105/#116 -- the perk read "your DoTs spread..."). The rework makes Haunt the
spec's button, and a button that eats a 1.5 sec cast on a spec built around
instant DoT application reads as broken. The instant must be per-player, not a
spell_dbc edit: zeroing Haunt's CastTimeEntry in the DBC (the Blizzard
PatchBlizzardServerSide pattern) would make Haunt instant for every warlock on
the realm, including Destruction/Demonology holders who never took the perk.

Mechanics: the callback runs at exactly the point CHEAT_CASTTIME lands -- after
CalcCastTime -- so hasted and cheat paths compose the same way and nothing
re-reads CastTimeEntry afterwards. Module side,
LivingGear_ClassPerks.cpp's LivingGear_SpellIsInstantCast gates on: caster is a
player, GetClassPerk == SPELL_WARLOCK_AFFLICTION (910157), and the spell's
chain head is SPELL_HAUNT (48181), so a future Haunt rank cannot regress.

The matching cooldown clear is module-side (ClearCooldownAfterCast, deferred
past Spell::finish) and needs no core change.

--- a/src/server/game/Spells/Spell.cpp
+++ b/src/server/game/Spells/Spell.cpp
@@ -103,6 +103,7 @@ bool LivingGear_BypassStealthRequirement(Unit* caster);
 // refunded afterwards -- a refund still requires the caster to have the power
 // to pay up front (LivingGear_ClassPerks.cpp).
 bool LivingGear_SpellIsFreeCast(Unit* caster, uint32 spellId);
+bool LivingGear_SpellIsInstantCast(Unit* caster, uint32 spellId);
 // Living Gear core-patch: does the account reagent vault cover this craft's
 // reagent requirement? Answers in place -- banked reagents count as
 // "in your backpack" for crafting, and nothing is moved (LivingGear_Vault.cpp).
@@ -3617,6 +3618,13 @@ SpellCastResult Spell::prepare(SpellCastTargets const* targets, AuraEffect const
         if (m_caster->ToPlayer()->GetCommandStatus(CHEAT_CASTTIME))
             m_casttime = 0;
 
+    // Living Gear core-patch 0030: an ability a class perk advertises as
+    // instant has its cast time zeroed here, after CalcCastTime, the same
+    // point where the CHEAT_CASTTIME override lands. See
+    // LivingGear_SpellIsInstantCast in mod-living-gear.
+    if (LivingGear_SpellIsInstantCast(m_caster, m_spellInfo->Id))
+        m_casttime = 0;
+
     sScriptMgr->OnSpellPrepare(this, m_caster, m_spellInfo);
 
     // don't allow channeled spells / spells with cast time to be casted while moving
